Patch 7918 (experimental, rollback netcode): the vendored psnr client is replaced by the re-psn v0.8.0 client, for the rollback rendezvous over re-psn.

The rollback rendezvous needs the real-time convention (psnr_relay_unwrap_from, psnr_rtt_ms / psnr_report_rtt, psnr_heartbeat, GET_CAPS, room parse helpers).
Source: https://github.com/undecuple/re-psn client/psnr.c and client/psnr.h at tag v0.8.0 (annotated tag object 61834bbe7cd2..., commit 57d41c27bd1b),
MIT (LICENSE of that repository; the same author as the toolkit's earlier source sp00nznet/psnr). The two files are byte-identical to that tag (compared with the
raw files of the tag); README.md names the new source.
API check against the callers in the runtime (np_psnr.c, cellNetCtl.c, sceNp.c, sceNpMatching2.c, sceNpScore.c): every function the callers use keeps its signature
(psnr_connect, psnr_poll, psnr_call, psnr_send, psnr_close, psnr_server_addr, psnr_probe_packet, psnr_punch_packet, psnr_probe_reply, psnr_is_control, psnr_relay_wrap,
psnr_relay_unwrap, psnr_stream_connect / accept, psnr_connect_error, psnr_msg_free; compared by declaration text) and the message / error enum values are unchanged; the
new header only ADDS functions, message types (PEER_AUTH, GET_CAPS, SET_ROOM_ACCESS, JOIN_BY_CODE, GET_ROOM_ACCESS, CAPS) and psnr_found. No caller needed a change.
Behaviour not verified by a run against a real server (see docs/ROLLBACK.md); the host test installer/tools/net_repsn_test.sh runs it against a fake server.

